        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(telegram): accept threadName as alias for name in topic-create/edit",
        "body": "## Summary\n\nThe MCP message tool uses threadName as the parameter name for topic-create and topic-edit, but the handler reads name. This causes ToolInputError when calling these actions via MCP.\n\n## Fix\n\nAdded threadName as a fallback alias for name in both createForumTopic and editForumTopic handlers in extensions/telegram/src/action-runtime.ts.\n\nBefore: const name = readStringParam(params, \"name\", { required: true });\nAfter:  reads name and threadName independently, uses ?? to pick whichever is set, throws only if both missing.\n\n## Root cause\n\nMCP schema uses threadName (consistent with other snake_case Telegram params); handler expects canonical name. Two separate validation layers that do not talk to each other.\n\n## Testing\n\nVerified locally: message action=topic-edit threadName=\"...\" threadId=286226 now returns ok: true instead of ToolInputError.",
